{"id":"2b923681-ecc1-49a5-9a00-5a0eb70c63a7","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"47f0a8514eb866be","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/explore.ts","baseline":{"blob":"9dbab2a3303bb7e16ec8b18224bf013cf32ce65b","start":0,"end":77},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","Control",",","Explored",",","Ordering",",","Printed","}","from","\"","../debug-protocol","\""]},"context":{"after":"f4c2ed6f308a6039"}},"payload":{"text":"Every ordering of the program's events (tsval's explore, packages/tsval/src/explore.ts): each run fresh, with the\nstand-ins a run of a given schedule has, so every host call answers at once, and which answer comes first, or whether\none comes before a timer, is the choice. No breakpoints, no stops. Each distinct ending: what it printed and where (a\ncrash too: a throw, or a rejection nothing handled), a schedule that gets there, and the events chosen along it.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:11:21.798Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:11:21.798Z"}
